cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite the accompanying PRABASI dataset paper."
title: "PRABASI: A Multi-Decadal Dataset of Socio-Economic Disparities and Interstate Migration in India"
version: "Anonymous peer-review version"
date-released: 2026
type: dataset
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
abstract: >
Modeling internal migration in the Global South is fundamentally bottlenecked by a lack of high-fidelity, longitudinal data. We introduce PRABASI, a multi-decadal dataset that integrates interstate migration and socioeconomic indicators across three Indian census cycles (1991–2011), providing a structured resource for data-driven analysis of interstate migration in India. Moving beyond traditional gravity models, PRABASI integrates 14 state-level socio-economic indicators that capture inter-regional disparities. Benchmarking with tree-based architectures yields robust performance ($R^2 = 0.88$) under rigorous temporal and spatial holdouts, significantly outperforming standard log-linear baselines. Crucially, our evaluations reveal that a combination of demographic, socio-economic, and geographical features exhibits profound predictive power, exposing distinct non-linear push-pull dynamics between male and female cohorts. PRABASI provides a validated, ML-ready foundation for uncovering the complex drivers of subnational migration in developing economies.
keywords:
  - migration
  - interstate migration
  - India
  - machine learning
  - socio-economic disparities
  - Census
  - computational social science
